    <h2>Practical Tips Before You Apply</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Use <a href="/australia/car-loan-calculator/">CalcPhi's Car Loan Calculator</a> to see your actual repayment and total cost — not just the monthly number the dealer quotes.</li>
      <li>Check your budget using <a href="/australia/budget-calculator/">CalcPhi's Budget Calculator</a> to confirm the monthly repayment fits without squeezing other financial goals.</li>
      <li>Compare the comparison rate across at least three lenders — it is a like-for-like benchmark.</li>
      <li>Consider a shorter loan term if you can afford higher repayments — a three-year loan at the same rate costs far less in total interest than a five-year loan.</li>
      <li>Avoid extending a car loan beyond five years — you risk being "upside down" on the loan (owing more than the car is worth) if you need to sell or refinance early.</li>
    </ul>


