    <h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
    <ul class="faq-list">
      <li class="faq-item">
        <h3 class="faq-q">Is it better to get a car loan or pay cash in Australia?</h3>
        <p class="faq-a">It depends on your interest rate versus what you could earn by investing the cash. If your car loan rate is 8% and your invested money would return 9–10% in shares, borrowing may come out slightly ahead over five years. But if you have no strong investment plan for the cash, paying outright is almost always cheaper and simpler.</p>
      </li>
      <li class="faq-item">
        <h3 class="faq-q">What is a good interest rate for a car loan in Australia in 2026?</h3>
        <p class="faq-a">In 2026, competitive secured car loan rates from banks and credit unions generally sit between 6.5% and 9% p.a. for borrowers with good credit. Always compare the comparison rate, not just the advertised rate, as it includes fees.</p>
      </li>
      <li class="faq-item">
